[TECHNICAL_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L3-ANS-007
TITLE: Qube kill
STATEMENT: >>>
When state ``destroyed`` is declared, the qube module shall kill the qube
without a graceful shutdown.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Event-driven
PRODUCT: Ansible
STATUS: Partial
RATIONALE: >>>
``admin.vm.Kill`` and ``admin.vm.Shutdown`` are separate endpoints, and no
argument to Shutdown destroys a running qube. The documented hard kill is
therefore reachable only through Kill, which the graceful path never calls.
<<<
DEFECT: >>>
``destroyed`` is normalised to ``halted`` and routed to the graceful shutdown
path, so the documented ``qvm-kill`` equivalent never reaches ``admin.vm.Kill``
(qubes-ansible/ansible_collections/qubesos/core/plugins/module_utils/qubes_module_qube.py:94).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L2-LIFECYCLE-05
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Implementation
  PATH: qubes-ansible/ansible_collections/qubesos/core/plugins/module_utils/qubes_helper.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesHelper.destroy
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Implementation
  PATH: qubes-ansible/ansible_collections/qubesos/core/plugins/module_utils/qubes_module_qube.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubeModule.__init__
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Authority
  PATH: qubes-core-admin/qubes/api/admin.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubesAdminAPI.vm_kill

