[TECHNICAL_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L3-ANS-013
TITLE: Tag configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The qube module shall bring the qube's tag set to the tags declared in the
``tags`` parameter.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Ubiquitous
PRODUCT: Ansible
STATUS: Partial
DEFECT: >>>
Tag handling is additive only — a tag present on the qube but absent from the
declared set is never removed, so a tag set cannot be converged
(qubes-ansible/ansible_collections/qubesos/core/plugins/module_utils/qubes_module_qube.py:363).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L2-CONFIG-05
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Implementation
  PATH: qubes-ansible/ansible_collections/qubesos/core/plugins/module_utils/qubes_module_qube.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: QubeModule.enforce_tags
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Verification
  PATH: qubes-ansible/tests/qubes/test_module_qube.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: test_properties_and_features_set_and_tag_vm

[TECHNICAL_REQUIREMENT]
UID: L3-ANS-014
TITLE: Tag removal command
STATEMENT: >>>
When the ``removetags`` command is issued, the command module shall remove every
listed tag from the qube.
<<<
EARS_PATTERN: Event-driven
PRODUCT: Ansible
STATUS: Partial
DEFECT: >>>
``contextlib.suppress`` wraps the whole removal loop, so the first tag that is
not present aborts every remaining removal
(qubes-ansible/ansible_collections/qubesos/core/plugins/module_utils/qubes_module_command.py:165).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: L2-CONFIG-05
  ROLE: Refines
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Implementation
  PATH: qubes-ansible/ansible_collections/qubesos/core/plugins/module_utils/qubes_module_command.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: remove_tags
- TYPE: File
  ROLE: Verification
  PATH: qubes-ansible/tests/qubes/test_module_command.py
  ELEMENT: function
  ID: test_removetags_errors_if_no_tags_present

